## For the lead

1. **Dose (pick: 48 lessons a year of 45 minutes, three every two weeks).** APPROACH.md says about 45; 48 gives a
   fixed rhythm a school can timetable and puts the checks on weeks 17 and 32. A school that adds time (the
   national figure is 80 hours a year; this is 36) adds lessons to extend units, never a new unit.
2. **After-core checks.** Health's checks sit in weeks 17 and 32 in grades 6, 7 and 8. `frame.py calendar` on
   2026-11-25 shows no clash with the after-core 6 to 8 frames written so far (grade 8 CTE uses weeks 16 and 32;
   week 32 is the shared finals week). Pick: keep, and recheck in the lead's one calendar pass.
3. **Row change made: g6-pa-habits-supports-barriers** gains `~NHES.S6.8.2` and one note sentence (the class
   activity goal set alone, with help or as a group), so standard 6 is practiced in two topics with the sensitive
   rows out, as the K to 2 pilot did for its physical activity row. Pick: add the same count note to STANDARD.md
   section 4 with the pilot's For the lead 4.
4. **Two grade 5 dead ends (both ends of the handoff, rows outside this band's end).** g5-fn-claims-that-hurt hands
   on to nothing although g7-fn-judge-claims judges fads (PHW 12); g5-s-online-safety hands on to nothing although
   g7-s-online-boundaries carries the online thread. Pick: g5-fn-claims-that-hurt hands_on `g7-fn-judge-claims`
   and g7-fn-judge-claims assumes adds it; g5-s-online-safety hands_on `g7-s-online-boundaries` and
   g7-s-online-boundaries assumes adds it. Each is two grades back, so units 13 and 14 would gain a readiness check
   in the last ten minutes of units 12 and 13. Not edited here: the grade 5 end is the grades 3 to 5 frame's.
