re (bar criterion 4) sits here, early, before the alcohol facts in unit 5. Influences come before food (unit 6) because the food pattern uses the influence check. SEL grade 6 unit 4 and unit 5 lean on this unit's rows (Cross-subject) | Candidate: HECAT T module 6-8 read may add "secondhand smoke and vapor"; one line on day 2 | No scare images, no worst cases as the usual outcome. A student who lives with someone who smokes or vapes is never made to feel blame; quitting help is named for any adult. A card plays the offer; no student plays the person offering. Agent reads: sensitivity (tobacco sources named in the brief) |
