436: ## For the lead
437: 
438: 1. **Dose (pick: 48 lessons a year of 45 minutes, three every two weeks).** APPROACH.md says about 45; 48 gives a
439:    fixed rhythm a school can timetable and puts the checks on weeks 17 and 32. A school that adds time (the
440:    national figure is 80 hours a year; this is 36) adds lessons to extend units, never a new unit.
441: 2. **After-core checks.** Health's checks sit in weeks 17 and 32 in grades 6, 7 and 8. `frame.py calendar` on
442:    2026-11-25 shows no clash with the after-core 6 to 8 frames written so far (grade 8 CTE uses weeks 16 and 32;
443:    week 32 is the shared finals week). Pick: keep, and recheck in the lead's one calendar pass.
444: 3. **Row change made: g6-pa-habits-supports-barriers** gains `~NHES.S6.8.2` and one note sentence (the class
445:    activity goal set alone, with help or as a group), so standard 6 is practiced in two topics with the sensitive
446:    rows out, as the K to 2 pilot did for its physical activity row. Pick: add the same count note to STANDARD.md
447:    section 4 with the pilot's For the lead 4.
448: 4. **Two grade 5 dead ends (both ends of the handoff, rows outside this band's end).** g5-fn-claims-that-hurt hands
449:    on to nothing although g7-fn-judge-claims judges fads (PHW 12); g5-s-online-safety hands on to nothing although
450:    g7-s-online-boundaries carries the online thread. Pick: g5-fn-claims-that-hurt hands_on `g7-fn-judge-claims`
451:    and g7-fn-judge-claims assumes adds it; g5-s-online-safety hands_on `g7-s-online-boundaries` and
452:    g7-s-online-boundaries assumes adds it. Each is two grades back, so units 13 and 14 would gain a readiness check
453:    in the last ten minutes of units 12 and 13. Not edited here: the grade 5 end is the grades 3 to 5 frame's.
454: 5. **g6-pa-habits-supports-barriers lean wording.** Its cross_subject says "after the grade 6 statistics unit", but
455:    math grade 6 unit 8 runs days 142 to 157, after this course's grade 6 goal unit. Pick: change it to
456:    "math:6.SP.B.5 (summarize a behavior log; health reads counts only when math is later)".
457: 6. **SEL and PE sides.** The SEL and PE 6 to 8 frames can cite health units by the tables above (SEL: units 2, 3,
458:    4, 7, 8, 11, 12, 17, 18, 23 to 27; PE: units 8, 16, 27). PE's g7-eat-move-well is named in unit 16.
459: 7. **Browser check.** The national highway traffic safety agency's car seat page returned 403 to the K to 2
460:    reader's fetcher, so its bicycle and impaired driving pages named here are marked browser check; the safety read
461:    opens them in Claude in Chrome.
462: 8. **Survey figures.** Units 4, 12 and 25 name the national youth tobacco survey and a national survey of grade 8
463:    students; the expert read enters each figure with its source and latest year. No download or sign-in is needed.
464: 9. **Supplies ceiling (money, Cory's).** Grade 6 $32, grade 7 $31 ($46 with a bought helmet), grade 8 $39 for a
465:    class of 30. Pick: $40 a year for a class of 30, with the optional helmet outside it.

