{"strand": "s", "grade": "7", "skill_id": "g7-s-spot-speak-up", "standard": "NHES.S8.8.1", "assumes": "g6-s-speak-up-for-others", "hands_on": "g8-s-advocacy-results", "model_in": "speak-up-plan", "model_out": "speak-up-plan", "words": "opportunity; family; community; advocate", "cross_subject": "", "notes": "Examine chances to speak up for the health of individuals, families and communities: a crosswalk, a school lunch, a heat plan. Students choose one real chance and write a one-line ask. Serves HECAT.S.HBO8."}
{"strand": "t", "grade": "7", "skill_id": "g7-t-advocate-alone-or-group", "standard": "NHES.S8.8.2", "assumes": "g6-t-nicotine-facts; g6-s-speak-up-for-others", "hands_on": "g8-fn-advocacy-audience; g8-pa-advocacy-practice; g8-t-tobacco-influences", "model_in": "speak-up-plan", "model_out": "speak-up-plan", "words": "advocacy; group; petition; policy", "cross_subject": "ela:W.7.1 (write an argument with claims and evidence)", "notes": "Decide whether to advocate alone or in a group for a given situation (a tobacco-free school, a vape-free event) and plan the first step. Serves HECAT.T.HBO3, HECAT.T.HBO4."}
{"strand": "meh", "grade": "7", "skill_id": "g7-meh-self-harm-help", "standard": "~NHES.S3.8.1; ~NHES.S4.8.3", "assumes": "g6-meh-stress-coping", "hands_on": "g8-meh-suicide-help", "model_in": "help-steps", "model_out": "help-steps", "words": "self-harm; crisis; 988; trusted adult", "cross_subject": "", "notes": "Sensitive unit (removable). Leave-out note and family note before it as STANDARD.md section 5 says; the disclosure steps are on the approach page. Teacher note: no method detail, no lesson without a help line and an adult plan; safe-messaging rules; a counselor knows a lesson is coming and is on call. Students learn signs a friend needs help, what to say and who to tell at once, and that it is never a secret to keep. The course still teaches support and help in g6-phw-adult-or-professional and g7-meh-seek-and-give-support (non-sensitive units). Students are not asked about their own feelings. Serves HECAT.MEH.HBO6, HECAT.V.HBO10."}
{"strand": "v", "grade": "7", "skill_id": "g7-v-dating-and-sexual-harassment", "standard": "~NHES.S4.8.4; ~NHES.S4.8.3", "assumes": "g6-v-unwanted-touch-and-help", "hands_on": "g8-v-dating-and-assault", "model_in": "boundary-steps; help-steps", "model_out": "boundary-steps; help-steps", "words": "dating; harassment; consent; abuse; help", "cross_subject": "", "notes": "Sensitive unit (removable). Leave-out note and family note before it as STANDARD.md section 5 says; the disclosure steps are on the approach page. The course still meets these skills in g7-s-online-boundaries and g7-meh-seek-and-give-support. Teacher note: leave-out note and family note. Healthy and unhealthy relationship signs, sexual harassment, consent as a clear freely given yes, and where to get help. Respect for every person; never blame. Students rehearse written refusal lines; cards play any pressure. Serves HECAT.V.HBO4, HECAT.V.HBO8, HECAT.V.HBO9."}
{"strand": "sh", "grade": "7", "skill_id": "g7-sh-relationships-consent", "standard": "~NHES.S4.8.4; ~NHES.S4.8.3", "assumes": "g6-sh-puberty-and-health", "hands_on": "g8-sh-prevention-and-health", "model_in": "boundary-steps", "model_out": "boundary-steps", "words": "relationship; consent; identity; abstinence", "cross_subject": "", "notes": "Sensitive unit (removable). Leave-out note and family note before it as STANDARD.md section 5 says; the disclosure steps are on the approach page. The course still meets these skills in g7-s-online-boundaries and g7-meh-seek-and-give-support. Teacher note: school or family decides; inclusive of every identity. Healthy relationships, consent, choosing not to have sex, never pressuring anyone, and respect for gender identity and sexual orientation. No scare tactics, no shame. Serves HECAT.SH.HBO2, HECAT.SH.HBO3, HECAT.SH.HBO4, HECAT.SH.HBO5, HECAT.SH.HBO9."}
{"strand": "s", "grade": "7", "skill_id": "g7-s-ride-gear-places", "standard": "~NHES.S1.8.3", "assumes": "g6-phw-prevent-illness-injury", "hands_on": "", "model_in": "", "model_out": "", "words": "passenger; seat belt; driver; helmet; gear; alone; dangerous place", "cross_subject": "", "notes": "Safety as students start riding with older drivers and going out alone (Cory, 2026-11-20): buckle up and ride in the back seat, never ride with a driver who has used alcohol or drugs or is driving unsafely, and plan another way home; wear the right gear for bikes, boards and scooters and wear it right; notice dangerous places (water, tracks, building sites, empty lots) and stay away. Students rehearse turning down a ride and calling for another one from written scripts; a card plays the driver, and no student plays an impaired driver. Serves HECAT.S.HBO1, HECAT.S.HBO2, HECAT.S.HBO3, HECAT.S.HBO6."}
{"strand": "phw", "grade": "8", "skill_id": "g8-phw-factors-shape-health", "standard": "NHES.S1.8.6; ~NHES.S1.8.1", "assumes": "g7-pa-influence-differs-by-group; g7-phw-living-with-conditions; g5-phw-surroundings-community", "hands_on": "g9-phw-strengths-wellness-links; g9-phw-factors-and-behavior; g9-phw-conditions-equity", "model_in": "influence-check", "model_out": "influence-check", "words": "personal; social; community; environmental", "cross_subject": "", "notes": "Analyze how personal, social, community and environmental factors each affect health, with a case such as asthma and air quality or sleep and school start time. Returns to g5-phw-surroundings-community after a skip: the idea is not taught in between, on purpose. Serves HECAT.PHW.HBO6."}
{"strand": "phw", "grade": "8", "skill_id": "g8-phw-health-care-services", "standard": "NHES.S1.8.7", "assumes": "g7-phw-health-literacy-links; g6-phw-adult-or-professional", "hands_on": "g9-phw-access-to-care", "model_in": "help-steps", "model_out": "help-steps", "words": "services; insurance; vaccine; checkup", "cross_subject": "", "notes": "Explain how health care services help keep a person healthy: checkups, vaccines, dental, vision, school nurse, urgent care and what each is for. Teacher note: access and cost differ. Returns to g6-phw-adult-or-professional after a skip: the idea is not taught in between, on purpose. Serves HECAT.PHW.HBO10, HECAT.PHW.HBO11."}
{"strand": "meh", "grade": "8", "skill_id": "g8-meh-tools-for-influences", "standard": "NHES.S2.8.4", "assumes": "g7-fn-influences-on-eating", "hands_on": "g9-meh-influences-judge-plan", "model_in": "influence-check", "model_out": "influence-check", "words": "influence; media literacy; tool; limit", "cross_subject": "", "notes": "Put methods and tools into practice to deal with what affects wellness: social media limits, ad analysis, a pause rule, talking with a friend. Students test a tool for a week with a log they keep private. Serves HECAT.MEH.HBO2, HECAT.MEH.HBO9."}
{"strand": "phw", "grade": "8", "skill_id": "g8-phw-handle-false-messages", "standard": "NHES.S3.8.5", "assumes": "g7-fn-judge-claims; g7-phw-credible-sources", "hands_on": "g9-fn-information-skill; g9-meh-counter-disinformation", "model_in": "source-check", "model_out": "source-check", "words": "misinformation; rumor; viral; fact-check", "cross_subject": "ela:RI.8.8 (evaluate an argument and its evidence)", "notes": "Use strategies for handling false and misleading health messages: stop, check the source, find a second source, tell what is false kindly. Students fact-check three posts. Serves HECAT.PHW.HBO10."}
{"strand": "meh", "grade": "8", "skill_id": "g8-meh-teamwork", "standard": "NHES.S4.8.7", "assumes": "g7-meh-seek-and-give-support", "hands_on": "g9-meh-communication-channels; g9-meh-teams-negotiate-views", "model_in": "listening-steps", "model_out": "listening-steps", "words": "team; role; share; cooperate", "cross_subject": "", "notes": "Work well with others in different settings: roles, giving credit, handling a person who does not help. Students plan a team health project. Serves HECAT.MEH.HBO8."}
{"strand": "v", "grade": "8", "skill_id": "g8-v-negotiate-compromise", "standard": "NHES.S4.8.8", "assumes": "g7-v-conflict-prevent-end", "hands_on": "g9-meh-boundaries-consent; g9-v-conflict-manage", "model_in": "conflict-steps; boundary-steps", "model_out": "conflict-steps; boundary-steps", "words": "negotiate; compromise; interest; fair", "cross_subject": "", "notes": "Use negotiation and compromise: say what each side needs, offer trades, agree on a fair plan; a limit is not up for negotiation. Serves HECAT.V.HBO1, HECAT.MEH.HBO3."}
{"strand": "meh", "grade": "8", "skill_id": "g8-meh-different-views", "standard": "NHES.S4.8.9", "assumes": "g7-v-conflict-prevent-end", "hands_on": "g9-meh-teams-negotiate-views", "model_in": "listening-steps; i-statement", "model_out": "listening-steps; i-statement", "words": "view; value; respect; disagree", "cross_subject": "", "notes": "Talk with people whose views or values differ: ask to understand, find common ground, disagree kindly. Students rehearse on a food example, a screen-time example and one example about a belief or custom, worded to stay neutral on faith. Serves HECAT.MEH.HBO7, HECAT.MEH.HBO8."}
{"strand": "meh", "grade": "8", "skill_id": "g8-meh-express-concern", "standard": "NHES.S4.8.10", "assumes": "g7-meh-seek-and-give-support", "hands_on": "g9-meh-help-and-concern", "model_in": "listening-steps; help-steps", "model_out": "listening-steps; help-steps", "words": "concern; care; support; check in", "cross_subject": "", "notes": "Show understanding and concern for others: noticing, a check-in line, offering help, knowing when to tell an adult. Serves HECAT.MEH.HBO8, HECAT.MEH.HBO7."}
{"strand": "aod", "grade": "8", "skill_id": "g8-aod-decision-supports-obstacles", "standard": "NHES.S5.8.5", "assumes": "g7-s-decision-process-use", "hands_on": "g9-t-decision-views-process", "model_in": "decision-steps", "model_out": "decision-steps", "words": "support; obstacle; level; policy", "cross_subject": "", "notes": "Name the supports and obstacles shaping a decision at different levels (friends, family, school, laws, ads) for a decision about alcohol or other drugs. Serves HECAT.AOD.HBO3, HECAT.AOD.HBO4."}
{"strand": "pa", "grade": "8", "skill_id": "g8-pa-decision-look-back", "standard": "NHES.S5.8.6", "assumes": "g7-pa-options-wider-effects", "hands_on": "g9-aod-weigh-options-plan; g9-s-decision-levels-barriers; g9-pa-measure-decisions", "model_in": "decision-steps", "model_out": "decision-steps", "words": "evaluate; result; adjust; learn", "cross_subject": "", "notes": "Assess how a health decision worked out for me and others, for a character and for a school activity, and what to change. Serves HECAT.PA.HBO1, HECAT.PA.HBO5."}
