## For the lead

1. **Dose (pick: 30 lessons a year, one a week, weeks 1 to 30).** This is APPROACH.md's default exactly; weeks 31
   and 32 hold core year-end checks in all three grades. The national figure for grades 3 to 12 is 80 hours a year;
   this is 15. A school that adds time adds a second weekly lesson to extend units, never a new unit.
2. **Grade 5 year-end check in week 28 with two respond days.** Each year has 30 days, and a check on day 29 would
   fall in week 29, a grade 5 social studies check week; the second respond day is the band look-back and grade 6
   handoff. Pick: keep. The other choice is one more grade 5 unit day and a check in week 29 if the lead's calendar
   pass moves that social studies check.
3. **Row changes made (my rows only).** Standard 6 was practiced only in personal health. Added `~NHES.S6.5.3` to
   g4-pa-warm-up (its activity week is a goal plan) and `~NHES.S6.5.5` to g5-pa-habit-practice (its log tracks
   progress), with a note line on each, so standard 6 is practiced in personal health and physical activity with the
   sensitive rows out. No handoff cell changed: every grade 2 to grade 3 pair and every grade 5 to grade 6 pair
   already agrees at both ends.
4. **After-core check clashes (CALENDAR.md rule 1), not moved here.** The lead's one calendar pass settles them;
   `frame.py calendar` after this frame's sync lists any for grades 3 to 5.
5. **SEL side, when its 3 to 5 frame is written.** SEL grade 3's I-statement frame takes health's words; health uses
   SEL's feelings chart, calm-down card and upstander plan. SEL's "stop-think-choose" and health's decision steps are
   two cards for related skills: pick, keep both and have each frame name the other's card on the shared rows above,
   since health's steps carry options and results that SEL's three words do not.
6. **PE side, when its 3 to 5 frame is written.** It can cite health units 1, 8, 15 and 19 for g3-active-outside,
   g4-skill-fitness, g5-food-drink and g5-fitt.
7. **Puberty in two lessons (grade 4 unit 14).** Two 30-minute lessons for body changes, hygiene and who to ask is
   thin. Pick: keep two (the rows' load, and it returns in unit 21); a school may add a lesson, and the unit plan
   names what that lesson holds.
8. **Supplies ceiling (money, Cory's).** Grade 3 $18, grade 4 $19, grade 5 $20 in printing; the optional snack day
   is the school's own food cost. Pick: the same $30 a year for a class of 30 as the K to 2 pick.
9. **Owed before the scope and sequence.** Each grade's unit planner reads the HECAT 2021 modules its units use, 3-5
   span (STANDARD.md section 3); no download or sign-in is needed (CDC pages are free). No page was fetched for this
   frame, so no browser check is listed; the links in Safety and Sensitivity reads are named from memory and opened
   at the safety and expert reads.

